  "source": {
    "title": "Portadown News, 23 May 1958, p. 1 (\"Ex-Mayor Defeated in Aldermanic Contest\"); initials from the Northern Whig, 23 May 1958, p. 7 (\"Unionists retain control on Portadown Council\")",
    "publisher": "Portadown News (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "every figure read from the page image"
  },
  "note": "Borough election polled Wednesday 21 May 1958 and counted in the Town Hall on Thursday 22 May: three aldermen (for six years) and twelve councillors, twenty-four candidates. Labels as printed: U Unionist, L Labour (Northern Ireland Labour Party), R Portadown Rent and Ratepayers' Association. The Portadown News prints surnames only; initials and the outgoing members (asterisked) are from the Northern Whig. Electorate 9,002; votes cast 5,401 (59.88 per cent). Councillors: the Unionists won eleven of the twelve seats, the other being retained by T. Newell of the Northern Ireland Labour Party; 230 spoilt councillors' papers. H. McCourt, elected as an Independent in 1952 and 1955, stood as a Unionist."
}
